<h3>What this shows</h3>

Ideal body weight (IBW) is a reference value derived from height and
gender. Clinicians use it as one input among many — alongside body
composition, waist measurements and blood markers.

<h3>How it is calculated</h3>

For heights of five feet and above, this calculator uses the Hamwi method.
Below five feet it applies the Broca index.

<h3>Reading your result</h3>

A range is shown alongside the single figure. Healthy weight is a band,
not a point.
